\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Kathy automated the querying of HumpoDB (\'93humpological database\'94 quickly became too tiresome) to quickly show the nodes between one record and Chanta\'92s. She also built queries to list and drill into graphs where Chanta was not the source;Hayley worked from the supposition these were incomplete, and organised investigations to complete the picture. But even incomplete, Kathy could see recurring evidence. \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The highest concentrations of Chilli were present in Elvisettes and those Elvi who had received Chanta\'92s blessing personally. Each degree of separation from Chanta exhibited lower Chilli concentrations than the closer degree. The correlation supported the hypothesis that Chilli was transmitted sexually, and that its effectiveness dwindled with each transmission.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Kathy put off analysing the first degree from Chanta cohort until sexual transmission became a firm hypothesis. The data were anonymised but that didn\'92t stop Kathy from speculating.\
She graphed the number of instances per week over time. Her first thought was the numbers were exaggerated, but even if they were, Kathy still saw patterns. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

