The pattern sharpened.\
Each recipient received only part of the viable vector carried by the person who infected them. They could transmit it again, but only part of what they themselves carried. With every further transmission the concentration fell.\
That was why the Humpenings had failed.\
Chanta had been right about sex.\
He had been wrong about arithmetic.\
By the sixth degree, there was often too little of the protective vector left to protect anybody from anything.\

